 it was  embedded in his face  they covered his real eye in tape and  added the bulging glass eye over it  so for the entire shoot he could only  see out of one eye  the magical eye was radio controlled by  a crew member who made it swivel around  but sometimes it would actually pop out  sponged the transfers onto my scalp and  face  seeing voldemort for the first time was  a huge undertaking because of how  enormous the fans expectations were for  that exact moment  in order to transform the handsome ray  finds  into the dark lord they used a  combination of makeup  and prosthetics the process took hours  but luckily he only had to do the full  transformation about 60 to 70 times  throughout the whole series  and about 50 of those times were for the  last two movies  rafe still wanted to be able to act  under it all so they covered his  eyebrows  reshaped his eyes added long creepy  fingernails and false teeth  but the transformation wasn't complete  until they removed his nose using cgi  sort of slightly translucent  vein like quality we all remember the  scene where harry breaks his arm playing  quidditch  and gilda roy lockhart comes along to  fix it but ends up removing all the  bones instead  well that wobbly boneless arm wasn't cgi  at all but was actually a prosthetic  that they actually  attached to the real daniel radcliffe  and guess what  he still has it along with a few pairs  of potter glasses  daniel said that he has that creepy fake  arm sitting in his attic  all these years later i don't seek them  out  when creating professor trelawny emma  thompson had the idea that  since she is always looking into the  future the divination teacher can't  really see where she is in the present  so they came up with her famous coke  bottle glasses  while they were perfect for making her  eyes look very funny and large  they were actually quite uncomfortable  as they magnified  everything around her you must look  beyond  for the enormous battle at hogwarts the  m